            {
              "example": "0.8",
              "help_en": "Controls the randomness and diversity of model responses. Specifically, the temperature value controls the degree of smoothing applied to the probability distribution of each candidate token during text generation. A higher temperature value flattens the probability distribution, allowing more low-probability tokens to be selected and making the generated results more diverse. A lower temperature value sharpens the probability distribution, making high-probability tokens more likely to be selected and the generated results more deterministic. Valid values: [0, 2). A value of 0 is not recommended",
              "help_zh": "用于控制模型回复的随机性和多样性。具体来说，temperature值控制了生成文本时对每个候选词的概率分布进行平滑的程度。较高的temperature值会降低概率分布的峰值，使得更多的低概率词被选择，生成结果更加多样化；而较低的temperature值则会增强概率分布的峰值，使得高概率词更容易被选择，生成结果更加确定。\n\n取值范围： [0, 2)，不建议取值为0，无意义",
              "name": "temperature",
              "options": [
                "--temperature"
              ],
              "raw_name": "temperature",
              "required": false,
              "type": "float"
            },
            {
              "example": "0.8",
              "help_en": "The probability threshold for the nucleus sampling method during generation. For example, if the value is 0.8, only the smallest set of the most likely tokens whose cumulative probability is greater than or equal to 0.8 is retained as the candidate set. Valid values: (0, 1.0). A higher value increases the randomness of the generated results, while a lower value increases the determinism",
              "help_zh": "生成过程中的核采样方法概率阈值，例如，取值为0.8时，仅保留概率加起来大于等于0.8的最可能token的最小集合作为候选集。取值范围为（0,1.0)，取值越大，生成的随机性越高；取值越低，生成的确定性越高",
              "name": "topp",
              "options": [
                "--topp"
